# @theshelter/signing lives in the GitLab Package Registry of the public project the-shelter/packages
# (see APIs.md → /v2/manifest.json). Anonymous install; nothing else is scoped here.
# The GitLab registry publishes only a sha1 `shasum` for a package (no `dist.integrity`), so package-lock.json pins the
# tarball with a sha1 integrity, the one entry without sha512 (2026-11-15 audit, FEED-SEC-2; tests/npm-install.test.ts).
# To verify the tarball: download the lock's `resolved` URL (curl -sSfL -o signing-0.1.0.tgz '<resolved>'), then
#   shasum -a 1 signing-0.1.0.tgz   # 831e0caa5d56e861133c233e28d8180339991bf3, the lock's sha1 in hex
#   openssl dgst -sha512 -binary signing-0.1.0.tgz | base64   # bNiKs8Ue…ygv4LKw== on 2026-11-16
# and compare the unpacked files (tar -xzf) with the package's source in the-shelter/packages; it has no install script.
# The lock may be re-pinned by hand to `sha512-<that base64>` (npm ci then checks sha512); an `npm install` that
# touches the package writes the registry's sha1 again.
@theshelter:registry=https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/86141814/packages/npm/
